+++ b/openspec/changes/archive/2026-10-21-add-hourly-rental/design.md
@@ -0,0 +1,14 @@
+## Context
+
+`quote`, `book` and `availability` share `parsePeriod` and `price` in `src/index.ts`; periods are currently required to be midnight UTC.
+
+## Decisions
+
+- Period parsing accepts a start and end on the hour (whole hours since the epoch). If the length is under 24 hours the period is hourly; otherwise both ends must also be midnight UTC, as before. Alternative: allow hour-aligned multi-day rentals, rejected as out of the request.
+- Hourly total is `hourlyPrice * hours`, no discount. An item with no `hourlyPrice` makes `price` throw, so `book` fails too and leaves no trace.
+- `hourlyPrice` is optional; when present it is validated like `dailyPrice` (non-negative safe integer).
+- `availability` reuses `parsePeriod`, so it accepts hourly periods; overlap logic is unchanged because it compares instants.
+
+## Risks / Trade-offs
+
+- Whole-day periods keep their behavior; the "not at midnight" rejection now applies only to periods of a day or more (e.g. a start at 10:00 with a 2-day end is rejected, 10:00 to 12:00 is accepted).
