@@ -0,0 +1,27 @@
+## Why
+
+Many visitors only want a board for an afternoon, and today they are turned away because rentals are by whole days only. Customers should be able to rent by the hour.
+
+## What Changes
+
+- `addEquipment` accepts an optional `hourlyPrice` (non-negative integer of cents): the cost of one hour.
+- A rental shorter than a day that starts and ends on the hour is priced at the hourly price for each hour.
+- An item without an hourly price cannot be rented by the hour: quoting or booking it for such a period is rejected.
+- Rentals of a day or more still run on whole UTC days and are priced as before.
+- Availability accepts the same periods as quotes.
+
+## Capabilities
+
+### New Capabilities
+
+None.
+
+### Modified Capabilities
+
+- `rental`: Equipment registration, Rental periods, Quote and Availability change.
+
+## Impact
+
+- `src/index.ts`: `Equipment` type, `addEquipment` validation, period parsing and the shared pricing step.
+- `test/rental.test.ts`: new tests.
+- Assumptions: no long-stay discount applies to hourly rentals (they are under a day). A period of a day or more that is not whole UTC days is still rejected, e.g. 10:00 to 10:00 the next day. Overlap checks already work on instants, so hourly bookings cannot double book and need no change.
